  "id": "COMPOUND:33280 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Sarcotrine A is shown to have a target relationship with both Raji and Hepatocyte cells, which are subsequently targeted by specific compounds. These compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one, are all linked to Neuropilin-2 through a target relationship. This suggests that Sarcotrine A may act through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of these compounds in target cells. The evidence points to a potential role for Sarcotrine A in influencing the expression or function of Neuropilin-2, likely through the regulation of downstream pathways involving these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on the activity of these compounds, which may be critical for the biological effects of Sarcotrine A.",
